{number: 84}
{title: I Know Whom I Have Believed}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] I know not why God’s wondrous grace to me He hath made [Bb7] known,
Nor [Eb] why, unworthy, Christ in love re-[Bb7] deemed me for His [Eb] own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
But [Eb] “I know whom I have believed,
And am persuaded that [Bb7] He is able
To [Eb] keep that which I’ve com-[Ab] mitted
Unto [Eb] Him a-[Bb7] gainst that [Eb] day.”
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] I know not how this saving faith to me He did im-[Bb7] part,
Nor [Eb] how believing in His Word wrought [Bb7] peace within my [Eb] heart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] I know not how the Spirit moves, convincing men of [Bb7] sin,
Re-[Eb] vealing Jesus thro' His Word, cre-[Bb7] ating faith in [Eb] Him.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Eb] I know not when my Lord may come, at night or noonday [Bb7] fair,
Nor [Eb] if I walk the vale with Him, or [Bb7] "meet Him in the [Eb] air."
{end_of_verse}
